Indicators inside a quoted scalar that closes on its line are no nesting: the nesting guard, which reads only the lines before one that might nest deeper than tree-sitter-yaml's scanner can hold, skips them, so a value of 201 `- ` in quotes doesn't hide the keys after it.
The value prints cut at 40 characters, with its quote closed after the `…`.
== args
input/a.yaml
== file input/a.yaml
x: "- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - "
y: 1
== stdout
input/a.yaml (2 lines)
[L1-L1] x: "- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -…"
[L2-L2] y: 1
== stderr
== exit 0
